<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Deliberately empty.

    The app is not sandboxed and never will be: ARCHITECTURE.html §11 rules the
    Mac App Store out because sandboxing fights arbitrary folders, Tailscale and
    a local MCP. Outside the sandbox an entitlement is a hole cut in the
    hardened runtime, not a permission gained, so the right number of them is
    none until something actually fails without one.

    Two things that look like they need one and do not: ScreenCaptureKit, which
    the checking harness uses to photograph the app, is gated by the user's
    Screen Recording permission rather than by an entitlement; and Sparkle,
    which on an unsandboxed app installs updates through a helper it signs and
    ships itself.
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
